     "text": "In fact, five of them – Ohio’s Jon Husted, Alaska’s Dan Sullivan, Kansas’ Roger Marshall, Nebraska’s Pete Ricketts and South Carolina’s Darline Graham, who only took office in July – have not cast a single vote in opposition to Trump over the past two years, according to a CQ Roll Call analysis of Senate votes on which the White House took a position. All five represent states that Trump carried in each of his three elections.",
